<title>JAPAN: Kyocera rises on change of trading unit.</title>
<headline>Kyocera rises on change of trading unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kyocera Corp continued to rise on Wednesday morning, extending their gains for a forth day, supported by the firm's announcement earlier this week that it plans to change its stock trading unit to 100 shares from 1,000 shares on February 3, 1997, traders said.</p>
<p>The ceramic packaging maker was up 10 yen at 7,930 yen at 0131 GMT, on volume of 189,000 shares.</p>
